# AutoBuild-H5000M-Openwrt feed configuration - mainline OpenWrt.
# NOTE FOR EDITORS: scripts/feeds strips comments with s/#.+$// and then skips
# blank lines. A lone "#" with nothing after it is therefore NOT a comment to
# that parser and dies with "Syntax error in feeds.conf.default". Every comment
# line here must have text after the hash.
# Upstream source is openwrt/openwrt (branch main, i.e. SNAPSHOT). The official
# OpenWrt feed repositories publish their development branch as master, which
# is what openwrt/openwrt's own feeds.conf.default references - keep that so
# the feeds stay in lockstep with the tree we build.
# Since OpenWrt 25.12 the package manager is apk, not opkg; CONFIG_PACKAGE_*
# symbols are unchanged and nothing here is ImmortalWrt-specific.

src-git packages https://github.com/openwrt/packages.git;master
src-git luci https://github.com/openwrt/luci.git;master
src-git routing https://github.com/openwrt/routing.git;master
src-git telephony https://github.com/openwrt/telephony.git;master
src-git video https://github.com/openwrt/video.git;master
# NOTE FOR EDITORS: the video feed IS listed.  It was removed once to reduce
# Kconfig recursive-dependency pressure after upstream dropped the
# AUDIO_SUPPORT/DISPLAY_SUPPORT gate (da6323e5, de2f69bf, c375123b), and that
# was a dead end: the cycle count (26 / 14 / 156 / 178 across the runs) has
# never predicted whether qmodem survives, and qmodem never appears in any
# cycle in the first place.  The real cause is upstream 6e638524 - see the
# OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION note in configs/upstream.env.  So the feed stays, and
# no feed-list edit fixes the drop.
# The wwand feed (ddimension/openwrt-repo) is kept as an unconditional line.
# The long explanation that used to sit here claimed the feed was what kept
# qmodem alive, on the strength of three runs in which "wwand present"
# correlated with "qmodem survived".  THAT WAS WRONG.  The fourth run killed
# it: with the feed restored and its packages installed, qmodem still dropped.
# The correlation was two data points wide and one of them was misread.
# The real cause is upstream and has nothing to do with this feed: see the
# OPENWRT_PINNED_REVISION note in configs/upstream.env.  Briefly, upstream
# 6e638524 reordered two calls in scripts/package-metadata.pl, and the group
# of packages that stops being written into tmp/.config-package.in as a result
# includes all of QModem.  No feed list changes that.
# Keep this line only because a wwand build needs the feed and switching it on
# and off per-target is one more moving part; a QModem build gets the feed
# installed and does not emit any of its packages.  Removing it changes
# nothing about qmodem, and the cycle count (26/14/156/178 across the runs) has
# never predicted the outcome.  Do not tune the feed list to chase it.
src-git wwand https://github.com/ddimension/openwrt-repo.git;main


